    "source_file": "plugins/fleet-acp.md",
    "body": "# Fleet ACP\n\nFleet ACP is an MIT-licensed bridge between Fleet and Agent Client Protocol v1.\nThe remote machine owns its ACP-compatible agent, account, model, and API keys.\nThe plugin only initializes that local process, creates a session, delegates a\nprompt, and returns streamed output through the existing Fleet task ticket.\nVersion 0.1.2 keeps this one-shot task ABI while enforcing hard request,\nconfiguration, ACP frame, update-count, and collected-output limits. It drains\nstderr without unbounded retention and propagates shutdown into nested ACP\nprocess groups before forcefully cleaning up the delegated process tree.\n\nInstall it by asking an AI connected to Fleet Tool to call `install_plugin` with\n`plugin_id` set to `fleet.acp`. The target Agent applies its device permit:\n`off` refuses, `ask` prompts locally, and `allow` installs without a second\nplugin confirmation. Release and executable SHA-256 checks remain mandatory."
