    "source_file": "plugins/fleet-transfer.md",
    "body": "# Fleet Transfer\n\n`fleet.transfer` is the official file-system adapter for Fleet's direct-only\nfile transfer path. Fleet core authenticates the account and endpoints, signs a\nshort-lived direct-session ticket, and requires one local authorization\ndecision on each endpoint. A device Agent applies its permit: `off` refuses,\n`ask` prompts locally, and `allow` authorizes without another plugin click.\nThe plugin then reads or writes one regular file through the generic bounded\n`fleet.plugin.peer.v1` ABI.\n\nFile bytes use a dedicated reliable WebRTC DataChannel. The Worker and Durable\nObject carry only authentication, signaling, status, and short-lived tickets.\nIf a direct connection cannot be established, the transfer fails instead of\nfalling back to WebSocket, Worker, R2, TURN, or another relay.\n\nVersion 0.2.1 keeps manifest, chunk/hash, resume, acknowledgement, and commit\ninside the two plugin endpoints' private `fleet.transfer.v2` DATA protocol.\nFleet core preserves opaque DATA frame boundaries and does not understand file\ntransfer. One file, SHA-256 integrity, verified resume checkpoints, safe\ncancellation, no-clobber publication, and idempotent completion retry backed by\na transfer-bound local receipt are supported. Directories, symbolic links,\nspecial files, overwrite, and cross-account transfer remain excluded.\nBoth endpoints enforce a 10 GiB default local file-size limit. The target also\nkeeps 1 GiB free by default and rechecks capacity while receiving; operators\nmay override either byte limit through the plugin process environment."
